.TH CHPC-BASH-HELPER 1 "2026-09-29" "CHPC_bash_helper 0.1.0" "Coastal HPC"
.SH NAME
chpc-bash-helper \- build bash scripts for airgapped RHEL/Rocky/Debian systems from a vetted template library
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B python3 -m chpc_bash_helper
.I command
.RI [ arguments ... ]
.br
.B chpc-bash-helper
.I command
.RI [ arguments ... ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B chpc-bash-helper
builds bash scripts on a machine with no network access and no AI model
involved at all. You either pick a template from its library and answer
a short series of questions, or describe what you want in plain English
and let it match your description against the library by keyword
overlap.
.PP
Every generated script is checked with
.B bash -n
(a syntax-only parse; nothing is ever executed) before it is written to
disk. Nothing here reaches the network on its own.
.PP
The tool itself is pure Python 3 standard library and runs on Windows,
RHEL, Rocky, and Debian alike. The scripts it generates are bash, meant
for your Linux targets; two templates
.RI ( package_baseline ", " firewall_baseline )
explicitly support both the RHEL/Rocky
.RI ( dnf / yum ", " firewalld )
and Debian
.RI ( apt ", " ufw )
command sets.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
List every template in the library: its id, title, description, and
tags.
.TP
.BI show " template-id " "[--raw]"
Show what a template asks \(em its variables, yes/no toggles, and
multiple-choice groups \(em without generating anything. With
.BR --raw ,
also print the template's raw, unrendered text.
.TP
.BI describe " \(dqdescription\(dq"
Rank every template by plain keyword overlap between
.I description
and each template's tags and title/description text, best match first.
Purely deterministic string matching; no model is involved.
.TP
.BI build " template-id " "[options]"
Build a script from
.IR template-id .
With no
.BR --var / --toggle / --toggle-group / --yes
flags, runs an interactive wizard that asks each question in turn,
shows a summary, and writes the script only after you confirm. With any
of those flags present, runs non-interactively instead, using supplied
values and falling back to each question's declared default for
anything not supplied.
.SH OPTIONS FOR "BUILD"
.TP
.BI --out " path"
Where to write the generated script. Defaults to
.IR template-id .sh
in the current directory.
.TP
.BI --var " NAME=VALUE"
Answer one variable non-interactively. Repeatable.
.TP
.BI --toggle " NAME=on|off"
Answer one yes/no toggle non-interactively. Repeatable.
.TP
.BI --toggle-group " NAME=VALUE"
Answer one multiple-choice group non-interactively, by the option's
value (see \fBshow\fP). Repeatable.
.TP
.B --yes
Accept every default and run non-interactively, even with no
.B --var / --toggle / --toggle-group
given.
.SH EXAMPLES
List everything available:
.PP
.RS
.EX
python3 -m chpc_bash_helper list
.EE
.RE
.PP
Find the right template from a description:
.PP
.RS
.EX
python3 -m chpc_bash_helper describe "drain a node and note why"
.EE
.RE
.PP
Build it interactively:
.PP
.RS
.EX
python3 -m chpc_bash_helper build node_drain_resume
.EE
.RE
.PP
Build it non-interactively, for a repeatable/scripted run:
.PP
.RS
.EX
python3 -m chpc_bash_helper build node_drain_resume \e
    --var "NODE_LIST=node042" \e
    --var "REASON=Low RealMemory investigation" \e
    --toggle "REQUIRE_CONFIRMATION=off" \e
    --toggle-group "SCHEDULER=slurm" \e
    --toggle-group "ACTION=drain" \e
    --out node042_drain.sh
.EE
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
An unknown template id, a malformed
.BR --var / --toggle / --toggle-group
value, a template failed its
.B bash -n
check, or the interactive wizard was cancelled (declined the final
"write it now?" prompt, or input ended early).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I chpc_bash_helper/library/*.json
Template metadata: title, description, tags, and declared
variables/toggles/toggle_groups.
.TP
.I chpc_bash_helper/library/*.sh.tmpl
The matching raw bash template text for each
.I *.json
file, with
.B {{VARIABLE}}
and
.B {{#TOGGLE}}...{{/TOGGLE}}
placeholders.
.TP
.I chpc_helper_core/
The shared engine (templating, wizard, matcher, CLI) this app is built
on -- must be copied alongside
.I chpc_bash_helper/
as a sibling directory.
.SH SEE ALSO
The full manual,
.IR CHPC_HELPER_SUITE_MANUAL.md ,
and this package's own
.IR README.md ,
both shipped alongside this tool, cover adding new templates to the
library and the full command reference in more detail than fits here.
.SH AUTHOR
Coastal HPC.
